    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p><em style=\"\\&#x27;box-sizing:\">This buff bestows the insight bonus and reflex saving throw bonus but can only be applied to the caster.</em></p><p>When another creature is the subject of the spell, you receive warnings about that creature. You must communicate what you learn to the other creature for the warning to be useful, and the creature can be caught unprepared in the absence of such a warning. Shouting a warning, yanking a person back, and even telepathically communicating (via an appropriate spell) can all be accomplished before some danger befalls the subject, provided you act on the warning without delay. The subject, however, does not gain the <a href=\"\\&quot;https://www.d20srd.org/srd/theBasics.htm#insightBonus\\&quot;\">insight bonus</a> to AC and <a href=\"\\&quot;https://www.d20srd.org/srd/combat/combatStatistics.htm#reflex\\&quot;\">Reflex saves</a>. </p><p></p><p> </p>"
